I now have a complete picture. Here is my thorough report.

## Summary of findings

Membership tier is computed in one place only — the MapStruct mapper `OwnerMapper.membershipTier(...)` — and it currently returns only `SILVER` or `BRONZE`. **`GOLD` is not implemented anywhere** (not in the mapper, not in the OpenAPI enum), yet an acceptance test expects it for a 3+-member household. That is the core gap. Details below.

---

## 1. Membership tier logic

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java
This is the sole computation site. It is invoked at DTO-mapping time (on read/response), not during the create pipeline. Fields it keys off (`namesakeCount`, `email`) are populated earlier by pipeline steps.

```java
@Mapping(target = "membershipTier", expression = "java(membershipTier(owner))")
OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);

/**
 * The owner's membership tier: 'SILVER' when the owner has a unique name (namesakeCount is
 * zero) and an email address is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'.
 */
default OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum membershipTier(Owner owner) {
    if (owner == null) {
        return null;
    }
    Integer namesakeCount = owner.getNamesakeCount();
    boolean uniqueName = namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0;
    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();
    return uniqueName && hasEmail ? OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.SILVER : OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.BRONZE;
}
```

There is no `GOLD` branch, and no household-size input to this method.

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml (lines ~2140-2150)
`OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` is generated from this schema. The enum only declares `SILVER` and `BRONZE`, so no `GOLD` constant exists to return:

```yaml
membershipTier:
  title: Membership tier
  description: >-
    The owner's membership tier: 'SILVER' when the owner has a unique name
    (namesakeCount is zero) and an email address is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'.
  type: string
  enum:
    - SILVER
    - BRONZE
  example: 'SILVER'
  readOnly: true
```
(`OwnerDto` / `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` are code-generated into `target/` from this file.)

---

## 2. householdId and the household concept

### Model field — /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java
```java
@Column(name = "household_id")
private String householdId;
// getHouseholdId() / setHouseholdId(...) present

@Column(name = "namesake_count")
private Integer namesakeCount;   // <- the input to membershipTier()
```
Owner extends `Person` (firstName/lastName) and also holds `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `Set<Pet> pets`.

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdNormalizer.java
Canonical household identity, shared by the pipeline. A household is `lastName` (lower-cased, whitespace-collapsed) + normalized `address`.
```java
public static String id(String lastName, String address) {
    return "H-" + sha256hex(key(lastName, address)).substring(0, 12).toUpperCase();
}
public static String key(String lastName, String address) {
    return normalizeName(lastName) + "\n" + AddressNormalizer.normalize(address);
}
```

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java
Pipeline step that stamps `householdId` when `sharesHousehold` is true. **Note it does not count members or set any tier** — it only assigns the shared id and re-saves existing members. This is the natural place household size could be computed, but nothing does so today.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) return;
    String key = HouseholdNormalizer.key(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    boolean joinsHousehold = false;
    String householdId = HouseholdNormalizer.id(owner.getLastName(), owner.getAddress());
    for (Owner member : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (!key.equals(HouseholdNormalizer.key(member.getLastName(), member.getAddress()))) continue;
        joinsHousehold = true;
        if (!householdId.equals(member.getHouseholdId())) {
            member.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(member);
        }
    }
    if (joinsHousehold) owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
}
```

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueHousehold.java
Rejects duplicate households unless `sharesHousehold` is true (throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` → 409). Uses the same `HouseholdNormalizer.key`.

Related household escalation files (409 wiring):
- /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdException.java
- /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler.java
- /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml

`sharesHousehold` request field is defined in openapi.yml (lines 2052-2060, "Not persisted"); `householdId` response field at lines 2119-2128.

Note: there are two parallel naming sets of owner functions in the directory (e.g. `NormalizeAddress`/`AddressNormalizer`, `AssignHousehold`/`HouseholdNormalizer`, `NormalizeEmail`/`EmailNormalizer`). The ones wired into the POST pipeline are listed in section 3.

---

## 3. Owner creation endpoint (POST /owners)

### The pipeline YAML — /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml
This is the only `owners.POST` pipeline file (there is no v2 POST; the v2 dir has only `owners.GET.yml` and `pets.GET.yml`). Full step order:

```
composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')

